  "raw_text": "255\n\nBawan lâka tikpara\n \n(v\n-\nimp)\n \n–\n \ndon’t lose humility, remain humble\n \n/ no pierda la humildad, permanezca\n\nhumilde\n\nTiks\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntext\n \n/ texto\n\n(Construct:\n \nTikska\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nTikska na\n \naisi ba baku…\n \n–\n \nLike this scripture says…\n \n/ Como dice esta escritura...\n)\n\nBaibil tikska\n \n–\n \nBible text, scripture\n \n/ Texto bíblico, escritura\n\nBaibil tikska nani\n \n–\n \nscriptures\n \n/ esc\nr\nituras\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n07/19\n):\n \nBaibil tikska nani wan sinska briaia\n \n–\n \nTo\n \nhave Bible texts in our mind; To have Bible texts\n\nmemorized\n \n/ Tener textos bíblicos en nuestra mente; Tener textos bíblicos memorizados)\n\nMan\nka\n \ntikska\n \nba\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nthe y\neartext\n \n/\n \nel\n \ntexto del a\nñ\no\n\n(Ex/Ej\n:\n \n2024 MANKA TIKSKA BA: “Sibrin ai dauki ba ra\n \nman ra yang kasak lukisni” (LAW. 56:3)\n)\n\nYu bani tikska\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nd\naily text\n \n/\n \nt\nexto diario\n\nTila\n \n–\n \namong\n, midst\n \n/ entre, medio\n\n(Construct:\n \nT\nili\n,\n \nT\nilam\n)\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nTila wina kum kum ba rilidian wala bri kan\n \n–\n \nSome from among (them)\n \nhad (were\n \nhaving)\n \nanother religion\n \n/ Algunos de\n\nentre ellos tenían (estaban teniendo) otra religión\n)\n\nTilak\n \n–\n \nthrough the midst of\n \n/ en medio de\n\nTilara\n \n–\n \namong, in among, during, in the midst\n \n/ entre, durante, en medio\n\n(Construct:\n \nTilira\n,\n \nTilamra\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-07/20-2 Korint 12:10\n):\n \nDîa muni “swira paskan lâka nani” tilara lilia kaia sip sa?\n \n–\n \nWhy are we able to be happy\nin the midst of insults?\n \n/ ¿Por qué podemos ser felices en medio de los insultos?)\n\nTilara dimaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto enter among, to get involved in\n \n/ entrar, inmiscuirse, participar, involucrarse en\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/19\n):\n \nPulitik bara war aiklabanka nani ba tilara yawan dimaia apia sa\n \n–\n \nWe must not get involved in\nwar and politics; We must be neutral\n \n/ No debemos involucrarnos en la guerra y la política; Debemos ser\nneutrales)\n\nTilivisan\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntelevision\n \n/ televisión\n\nTilwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become mature, to ripen, to become full\n \n/ madurar, llenarse\n\nTilwan\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nfully grown, ripe, mature\n \n/ completamente crecido, maduro\n\nTimoti\n \n(\ndb,dba,dbta\n;\n \nTimotira\n-lrw\n)\n \n–\n \nTimothy\n \n(Bible books) / Timoteo (libros bíblicos)\n\nTim\n \n(\ndb,dba,dbta,dict\n,\ndictu\n;\n \nTem\n-\ndict-alt\n;\n \nTem\n-lrw\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \ntame\n \n/ domar\n\nDaiwan tim\n \n(a/t:\n \nDaiwan tem\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndomesticated (tame) animal\n \n/ animal domesticado\n\nTim daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto make tame\n \n/ hacer domesticar\n\nTim takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto become tame\n \n/ volverse manso\n\nTin\n \n(\ngpm\n-from English / de inglés;\n \nTen\n-mba\n) (Formerly/Anteriormente:\n \nMatawalsip\n)\n \n–\n \nten\n \n/ diez\n\nTingki\n \n(a/t:\n \nTengki\n-\ndict,dictu\n)\n \n–\n \nthanks, thanks to\n \n/ gracias, gracias a\n\n(Construct:\n \nTingkiki\n;\n \nTingkikam\n;\n \nTingkika\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh53\n):\n \npri sakaia pura mana aibapan ba tingki, ...\n \n–\n \nthanks to the paid ransom,...\n \n/ gracias al rescate pagado,...)\n\nTingki daukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto express thanks, to give thanks, to express gratitude\n \n/ expresar gracias, dar gracias,\nexpresar gratitud\n\nTingki lukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto think in an appreciative way, to be thankful\n \n/ pensar de manera apreciativa, estar\nagradecido\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-05/19\n):\n \nDîa dukiara yawan tingki lukisa?\n \n–\n \nFor what are we thankful?\n \n/ ¿De qué estamos agradecidos?)\n\nTingki pali\n \n–\n \nthank you very much\n \n/ muchas gracias\n\nTingki wiaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto thank, to say “thank you”\n \n/ agradecer, decir \"gracias\"\n\nTingkika lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngratitude, thankfulness, appreciation\n \n/ gratitud, aprecio\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-11/20\n):\n \nNahki yamni wan munisa wan tingkika lȃka Jehova ra marikaia ba\n?\n \n–\n \nHow does the showing of our\ngratitude to Jehovah benefit us?\n \n/ ¿Cómo nos beneficia mostrar nuestra gratitud a Jehová?)\n\nTingkikam lâka\n \n(\nbh,lv\n; alt:\n \nTingkikam\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nyour gratitude, your appreciation\n \n/ tu gratitud, tu aprecio\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nbh26\n):\n \nTingkikam marikaia dukiara,...\n \n–\n \nIn order to show your appreciation,...\n \n/ Para mostrar su\nagradecimiento,...)\n\nTingkika lâka\n \ntara\n \n(\nbh\n; a/t:\n \nTingkika tara\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \ndeep gratitude\n \n/ profunda gratitud\n\nTingkikas\n \n–\n \nwithout thanks\n \n/ sin gracias\n\nTingkikas kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be unthankful\n \n/ ser ingrato",
